Subject: [PATCH 10/19] kcm: Add and remove the custom modes of a screen

Where the compositor offers custom modes (libkscreen's Capability::CustomModes), a Custom
modes row under the refresh rate lists those of the screen, with a button to remove each,
and has fields for a width, a height and a refresh rate in hertz, with reduced blanking if
wanted, and an Add button. The mode is asked of KWin when the settings are applied, and
then shows under Resolution. A custom mode that is already there is not added twice, and
the sizes and rates are bounded as kscreen-doctor's addCustomMode leaves them open. What
is changed counts as something to apply.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
